// while and break. A loop is: the condition, a jz past the loop, the body, a
// yield (the scheduler's chance to run another script, once per iteration)
// and a jmp back to the condition. A break is a jmp whose target is not yet
// known: it goes on the stack bkg_brk, and the loop's end points every break
// above the height the loop started at (kept in the compiler's bkk_st_brk
// register, bkk_st_nobrk when no loop is open) to the instruction after it.

